<hr id="read-marker">
Dornwich is currently governed by the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">Old Reformist Party</span> (<span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>) under Bevan Hale (formerly of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>), leading a majority coalition that includes all parties positioned between the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, including the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and various <span style="color: #b8996f;">special</span> <span style="color: #11DD11;">interest</span> parties.

The Dornish Dispute arose when the Dornish branch of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> clashed with the party’s parliamentary delegation, demanding that Hale dissolve the Unity Coalition and negotiate with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>—even after the Commonwealth intervention. This conflict led to the party’s reformists breaking away and forming the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>, which has since evolved into a left-wing nationalist offshoot of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. Despite initially securing a majority of the state Assembly delegation following the dispute, the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> has struggled to achieve electoral success and now appears destined for irrelevance.

Notable members of the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> include Bevan Hale, August Winmore (a supporter of the officers’ putsch), Lorcan Underthorn (a "<span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #700000;">bolshevik</span>"), and its party leader, former Minister-President Kerrick Brunmoor. The party was labeled "<span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntist</span>" by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, marking the <span class="tooltip-text" title="that's me! the modman!">origin</span> of the term.
<hr id="read-marker">
United Left Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #C43988;">**KPO**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?]): [+ left_coalition_saxony +]% 

Unity Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if unionist_r_saxony:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> ?][? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]): [+ marcher_coalition_saxony +]% 

Propertied Coalition ([? if aspd_r_saxony: <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> + ?][? if unionist_r_saxony: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #11DD11;">**AGL**</span> + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**ECP**</span> + <span style="color: #0075EB;">**PRP**</span>[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>): [+ true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony +]%

Right-Wing Coalition ([? if aspd_r_saxony: <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> + ?][? if unionist_r_saxony: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #11DD11;">**AGL**</span> + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**ECP**</span> + <span style="color: #0075EB;">**PRP**</span>[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> + <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>): [+ bourgeois_coalition_saxony +]%

[? if royalist_saxony_elections_vote >= 4: The rise of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is quite unexpected, especially given their meager 1.6% of the vote in the last election. ?]

@saxony_achievement
go-to: alt_aber_gold if aspd_saxony_elections_vote >= 5 and saxony_election_seen == 1; saxony_coalition_menu if aspd_saxony_elections_vote < 5 or saxony_election_seen != 1

@alt_aber_gold
achievement: alt_aber_gold
go-to: saxony_coalition_menu

@saxony_coalition_menu
on-arrival: {!
let dvp_toleration_threshold = 50;
let lvp_toleration_threshold = 60;
if (!Q.gold_reform) {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 5;
} else if (Q.gold_reform) {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology != "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_ideology == "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology != "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.left_coalition_saxony >= 50) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation >= dvp_toleration_threshold && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= lvp_toleration_threshold && Q.lvp_formed)) {
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 0;
}
if (((Q.unionist_relation >= 50 || !Q.stegerwald_path) && ((Q.gold_relation >= (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed)))) {
    Q.marcher_coalition_possible_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.marcher_coalition_possible_saxony = 0;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation < (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation < (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed)) {
    Q.gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony = 0;
}
!}

<hr id="read-marker">
The propertied parties have historically been hostile to us in state politics, particularly after the notorious <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>-<span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> United Left government faced a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> six years ago. The split of our reformist wing into the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> further pushed our state organization toward the left.

[? if aspd_saxony_elections_vote <= 3: With the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>'s disastrous result of [+ aspd_saxony_elections_vote +]%, their viability as a political force in the state is coming to an end, with propertied parties are seeking a replacement for Bevan Hale. ?][? if aspd_saxony_elections_vote > 3: The <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> has not suffered the decline we thought it would, winning [+ aspd_saxony_elections_vote +]% of the vote. Whether Bevan Hale remains is up to the propertied parties. ?] Despite our cooperation on the local level, the national <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is unlikely to ever accept a coalition.

- @true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony
- @bourgeois_coalition_saxony
- @grand_coalition_saxony
- @united_left_saxony
- @no_majority
- @spd_majority


@toleration_saxony
title: We will enter a toleration agreement with the incumbent government.
choose-if: toleration_possible_saxony and left_strength < 30
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not toleration_possible_saxony: The propertied parties won't even accept our toleration. ?][? if left_strength >= 30: Our Dornish organization is too left-wing to even consider this as an option. With the reformists having largely split into the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">ORP</span>, the left wing is dominant. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_toleration = 1; guild_royalist -= 1; landed_royalist -= 1; commons_marcher += 1; commons_collectivist += 2; left_dissent += 10

We have entered a toleration agreement with the propertied cabinet, and have made it unnecessary for them to cooperate with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. As part of our agreement, the propertied parties have allowed Bevan Hale to retain his Minister-President position, and for the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> to occupy the Work and Welfare	ministry. 

Despite the unsavory qualities of the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>, they're still Vaelist at the end of the day. The leftist Dornish organization has protested at our intervention, and many have jumped ship to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony
title: The incumbent Hale III cabinet will continue.
subtitle: They are able to retain their majority. Surprising.
view-if: true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50
on-arrival: saxony_right = 1; saxony_leader = "Hale"; pro_republic += 1; landed_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_other += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_other += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; landed_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"

The surprisingly good results for the incumbent coalition[? if aspd_saxony_elections_vote >= 4:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>?] have allowed them and Hale to continue governing. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is discouraged by this defeat, as they had hoped to use their gains to influence the government.

@bourgeois_coalition_saxony
title: A propertied coalition is formed.
subtitle: The incumbent coalition, which will survive on toleration from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50 and true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50
on-arrival: saxony_right = 1; saxony_leader = "Brunwell"; saxony_irl = 1

The incumbent coalition has failed to win a majority, and toleration from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is required. They've demanded the exclusion of the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>[? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] from the cabinet, and the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]'s new Minister-President Dorian Brunwell has no choice but to agree. However, this decision was soon reverted and the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> is granted the Ministry of Work and Welfare. 

Despite the exclusion of many supporting parties from the cabinet in favor of non-partisan figures, they choose to tolerate the coalition nonetheless.

@grand_coalition_saxony
title: A [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition is formed!
subtitle: We have somehow reconciled with the propertied parties, that they're willing to govern with us again.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_relation < 50 and stegerwald_path: We need higher relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony: We need higher relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?]. ?][? if left_strength >= 15: Our Dornish organization is too left-wing to even consider this as an option—after all, their stubborn refusal in the past led to the expulsion of the majority of the parliamentary faction and the subsequent formation of the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">ORP</span>. ?]
view-if: marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50
choose-if: marcher_coalition_possible_saxony and left_strength < 15
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_groko = 1; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; unionist_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; gold_relation += 5; pro_republic += 3; reformist_dissent -= 15; reformist_strength += 10; aspd_dead = 1

Somehow, the propertied parties are willing to form a [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition with us, rather than continuing their current government with Bevan Hale and the right-wing parties.

With the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> (whose Dornish chapter is notably more sane) now convinced of our reformist path, they have rejoined the Dornish <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>!

@united_left_saxony
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> will form a coalition government with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
subtitle: History will repeat itself.
view-if: left_coalition_saxony >= 50 and (collectivist_relation >= 35 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or (collectivist_relation >= 55 and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators")
on-arrival: red_saxony = 1; unionist_relation -= 7; ddp_relation -= 7; gold_relation -= 7; lvp_relation -= 7; coup_progress += 5; dufour_angry += 60; vanguard_militancy += 0.08; vanguard_strength += 150; loyalist_strength += 80; warden_strength += 80; strife += 1; commons_marcher += 5; commons_collectivist += 5; disfavored_marcher += 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; guild_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 5; communist_coalition += 3; collectivist_relation += 15
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/redsaxony.png";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

Surprisingly, despite reluctance on both sides due to fears that the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> DuFour will order a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> if a coalition were to form, <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Dornwich is restored! 

As one of the most left-wing and industrial states in the Commonwealth, we will use our leverage to implement comprehensive reforms and transform Dornwich into a stronghold of <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>. DuFour’s patience is especially thin. Tread carefully.

@no_majority
title: No majority can be found!
subtitle: [? if bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and marcher_coalition_saxony < 50: All possible coalitions lack a majority. ?][? if marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and not marcher_coalition_possible_saxony: The propertied parties are antagonistic to our Dornish organization. ?][? if marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and left_strength >= 15: Our party itself rejects the possibility of a majority coalition with the liberals. ?]
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and (not marcher_coalition_possible_saxony or left_strength >= 15)
on-arrival: {!
let dvp_toleration_threshold = 30;
let lvp_toleration_threshold = 40;
if (!Q.gold_reform) {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 5;
} else if (Q.gold_reform) {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology != "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_ideology == "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology != "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.united_left_saxony >= 50) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
}
if (Q.saxony_no_majority) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold = 0;
    dvp_toleration_threshold = 0;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation >= dvp_toleration_threshold && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= lvp_toleration_threshold && Q.lvp_formed)) { 
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 0;
}
!}

With the propertied parties unable to secure a majority even with the toleration of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, and their refusal to form a coalition with us, no viable majority can be established. The ruling coalition fears that calling new elections will only accelerate their decline and further erode their support.

In an effort to avoid this, they are more open to negotiating a toleration agreement.

- @toleration_saxony
- @no_majority_2

@no_majority_2
title: A majority still can't be found!
subtitle: [? if not toleration_possible_saxony: This is getting ridiculous. ?][? if toleration_possible_saxony: We will refuse to tolerate the propertied government, forcing new elections. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_election_2_trigger_time = time + 3; saxony_no_majority = 1 if not saxony_no_majority; saxony_no_majority += 1 if saxony_no_majority; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 1; disfavored_royalist += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2 if toleration_possible_saxony; guild_marcher -= 2 if toleration_possible_saxony; landed_marcher -= 1 if toleration_possible_saxony

A coalition of all the parties to the right of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> isn't possible, and the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] is refusing any form of a Unity Coalition including us.

With no viable alternatives, the state Assembly faces dissolution, triggering new elections—an opportunity the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> hopes to exploit by capitalizing on political instability and the perceived failure of parliamentary democracy.

[? if saxony_no_majority > 1: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 2: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 3: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 4: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 5: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 6: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 7: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 8: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 9: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 10: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 11: Please stop. ?][? if saxony_no_majority > 12: Please stop. ?]

@spd_majority
title: Form an Marchers only government!
subtitle: Sweat...
view-if: marcher_r_saxony >= 50 
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 30; left_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; labor_dissent -= 10; aspd_dead = 1; commons_marcher += 7; commons_collectivist -= 4; burgher_marcher += 3; guild_marcher += 2; disfavored_marcher += 4; disfavored_royalist -= 3; pro_republic += 5

Unexpectedly, we've found ourselves controlling a majority of the Dornwich landtag and being able to form a government of just the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>! It is unclear how the propertied and <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span> will react to a <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Dornwich but without the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>... [? if aspd_share > 0: The <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> seeing as we no longer require on coalition negotiations to form government has decided to join us. ?] 
